      "usage": "derision, laughter(-ed to scorn, -ing), mocked, sport.",
      "full": "H7814. sechoq שְׂתוֺק שְׂחֹק, noun [masculine] laughter, derision, sport (properly infinitive construct); — absolute שְׂחֹק Jer 48:26 5 t.; construct Eccl 7:6 ; absolute שְׂחוֺק Jer 20:7 7 t.; — 1 laughter (joyous) Job 8:21 (|| תְּרוּעָה ), Psa 126:2 (|| דִנָּה ), Eccl 2:2 (|| שִׂמְחָה ), 10:19 (|| שִׂמֵּחַ ); as hollow Prov 14:13 (opposed to כָּאַב ), Eccl 7:3 (opposed to כַּעַס ), compare ׳שׂ הַבְּסִיל 7:6 . 2 (object of) derision, לִשׂ ׳הָיָה , Jer 20:7 ; 48:26-27 , (read ׳לִשׂ for ᵑ9 ᵑ6 ᵐ5 ׳הַשּׂ ᵑ0 Gie Du; Co strike out vv), 48:39 ; Lam 3:14 ; elsewhere Job 12:4 (twice in verse) 3 sport Prov 10:23 .",
